From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] android: link the display vout plugin with GLES2

Our Android CI builds now reach the native VLC module link stage on all three
architectures, but `libandroid_display_plugin.la` fails with unresolved OpenGL
ES symbols:

  undefined symbol: glClearColor
  undefined symbol: glClear

`modules/video_output/android/display.c` includes `<GLES2/gl2.h>` and directly
calls those functions when clearing the surface, yet its Automake rule only
links `$(LIBDL)`. Link it with `$(GLES2_LIBS)` like VLC's other GLES2-backed
video output modules.
---
 modules/video_output/Makefile.am | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/video_output/Makefile.am b/modules/video_output/Makefile.am
index 6d75a1d..014fa42 100644
--- a/modules/video_output/Makefile.am
+++ b/modules/video_output/Makefile.am
@@ -406,8 +406,8 @@ libandroid_display_plugin_la_SOURCES = video_output/android/display.c \
 	video_output/android/display.h \
 	video_output/android/utils.c video_output/android/utils.h
 libandroid_display_plugin_la_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS)
-libandroid_display_plugin_la_LIBADD = $(LIBDL)
+libandroid_display_plugin_la_LIBADD = $(LIBDL) $(GLES2_LIBS)
 
 libglconv_android_plugin_la_SOURCES = video_output/opengl/converter_android.c \
 	video_output/opengl/converter.h
